    cor:sha256 "ac66b478e20e82d4adede719c04a85f2071d5d5f005876b04851b94a76da2021" ;
    cor:pages 1 ;
    # [[R211]], 2026-09-13 — step (1) of the route off the hold recorded in the 2026-08-20 note
    # below: "author a cor:contract / cor:terms / cor:shapes triple for it — it carries none
    # today, so tests/test_corpus.py::test_grounding_where_contracted does not parametrize this
    # document at all and its grounding leg is entirely unexercised." It is parametrized from
    # here on. Step (2) — that test passing — is MEASURED: 189 records, 392 grounded, 377 still
    # quarantined, and the promotion membrane conforms. Step (3), a reviewer reading the carried
    # grid against the source page, remains the maintainer's and is deliberately NOT recorded
    # here; cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned.
    cor:contract "examples/shipping/capacity-contract.ttl" ;
    cor:terms "examples/shipping/capacity-terms.ttl" ;
    cor:shapes "examples/shipping/capacity-shapes.ttl" ;
    cor:expectedVerdict cor:CompilesAbove ;
    # 0.99, NOT the measured 1.0000. [[R194]] records that this document's score is exactly 1.0,
    # which is also how this repo writes a ratio ceiling — pinning it would refuse any future
    # escalated token whatever. The page carries 406 tokens, so 0.99 tolerates four tokens of
    # drift and still catches any systematic regression. Deliberately at-or-below the measured
    # score, never the measured value itself, as this file's header requires.
    cor:scoreFloor "0.99"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5 (agent), task 5 of the 2026-08-20 arc-denominator loop; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD — recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. Escalation-reason census 2026-08-20 (HEAD 820ab24), § Seam 1: score 1.0000, 1 page, ZERO escalation records on any of the nine reasons. § Token accounting for the same run reads 390 asserted / 0 escalated tokens — the only document in the corpus whose token ledger is clean. A SCORE IS NOT AN ACCEPTANCE: 1.0000 says nothing escalated, not that what was carried is what the page says, and no one has read this compile against the PDF. This is the corpus document nearest to acceptable, so the path to accepting it is named here rather than left implicit, and the rung has a route off 1/7: (1) author a cor:contract / cor:terms / cor:shapes triple for it — it carries none today, so tests/test_corpus.py::test_grounding_where_contracted does not parametrize this document at all and its grounding leg is entirely unexercised; (2) that test passing, so every grounded node stands behind exactly one accountable promotion; (3) a reviewer reading the carried grid against the source page and saying so in a dated note. Until all three, held." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5 (agent), the 2026-09-13 span-donation loop that closed R211; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD LIFTED, and the third step was discharged BY MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN BY EYE — a departure from how the 2026-08-20 note worded it, recorded here rather than glossed. That note named three steps. (1) A cor:contract / cor:terms / cor:shapes triple now exists (examples/shipping/capacity-{contract,terms,shapes}.ttl). (2) test_grounding_where_contracted passes: 189 records, 392 grounded, 377 still quarantined, and the promotion membrane conforms, so every grounded node stands behind exactly one accountable promotion. (3) The note asked for a reviewer reading the carried grid against the source page. What was done instead is four independent measurements of the port association, because the maintainer declined to accept a check the agent had delegated to them and was equipped to run: SHACL tiling (16 leaf columns covered exactly once, partition 1,1,2,2,2,2,2,2,2); the distribution against pdftotext -layout measured in an earlier loop, all seven figures identical; every entry cell's bbox inside the drawn interval of the port heading it, 406 of 406; and — the one that retires the by-eye question — assigning every data word to a port by nearest PRINTED LABEL INK, using no drawn rules at all, reproducing the drawn-interval assignment exactly, 406 agree and 0 disagree, with every label wholly inside its interval and centred to within about 1pt. The artifact is docs/superpowers/2026-09-13-graincorp-capacity-carried-grid.md. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: no tonnage is grounded — under the abstaining battery proposer ship:capacity grounds 0 of 189, so the tonnages are CARRIED and not asserted; 25 of 27 rows carry no year (R215); and R213 is now MEASURED at 110 of 110 zero-reading cells being invisible glyphs, dark navy on dark navy, which means the grid's zeros are empty cells on the page — a defect of the source reading, not of the span donation, and it stays open because what to emit for an invisible glyph is a CLAUDE.md section 8 classification. cor:scoreFloor is 0.99 rather than the measured 1.0000 for R194's reason: 1.0 is indistinguishable from a ratio ceiling, and at 406 tokens 0.99 tolerates four tokens of drift while catching any systematic regression." ] .

