        cor:rationale "HOLD — recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. Escalation-reason census 2026-08-20 (HEAD 820ab24), § Seam 1: score 0.9047, 1 page, ZERO escalation records on any of the nine reasons. The record count is the WRONG INSTRUMENT for this document, and that is the substance of the hold: § Token accounting for the same run reads 816 asserted / 86 escalated tokens, and the census states those 86 sit inside asserted regions and mint no record (compile.py:960 accrues escalated_total on a path that makes no escalate_region call). So cbh-stem has a real escalation surface of 86 tokens that is INVISIBLE to any count over escalation records, and the 0.9047 score is the only place it shows. Unlike graincorp-capacity this document does carry cor:contract / cor:terms / cor:shapes, so its grounding leg is exercised; what is missing is a reading of WHERE those 86 tokens went and whether losing them loses anything the page asserts. Held until that is measured, not until the score moves." ] ;
