        cor:rationale "HOLD, NOT LIFTED — cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. This note does not supersede the 2026-08-20 note above, which is NOT repaired in place; it records what moved and what did not since. The R261 totals-family loop (docs/superpowers/2026-10-01-r261-totals-family-evidence.md) shipped table-level totals: the four roster port totals (374,904 / 737,289 / 660,363 / 178,708), previously `#ignored` one-line bands booking 0/0 tokens, are now carried as `tab:PrintedTotal` nodes, each bound to its own panel's region by `tab:totalOf` and to its summed column by `tab:aggregates` (10/16/14/5 operand cells, exact Decimal match), under a `dec:produced` promotion decision gated on BOTH a NEURAL worker's `yes` AND exact arithmetic (evidence §§ 6.0 R47/R77, 7.4). The document's score moves 0.9103232534 -> 0.9106957425 and its triple count 13427 -> 13624 (evidence § 7.1); all six other corpus documents are byte-identical. The grand total `1,951,264` and the four-line Note beneath it — page 0 band 9 — are UNCHANGED: still one `KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED` escalation, 0 asserted / 86 escalated tokens, `table_uri None` (evidence §§ 1.2, 7.3, 7.4 — byte-for-byte identical to the pre-loop baseline), and the escalation-furnish pin (`tests/etkl/test_escalation_furnish.py::test_corpus_cbh_furnishes_exactly_one_request_for_its_one_live_escalation_the_residue`) still reads `live=1, requests=1`, unmoved. This is NOT an oversight: controller ruling R4 (evidence § 7.3) dropped total-of-totals binding from the loop entirely after Task 1's P3 probe REFUTED it (evidence § 6.4) — asked over the same cropped image, the grand total was not stably answered `yes` (`yes yes cannot_tell`, 2 of 3) and three of the four port totals themselves drew at least one `yes` to 'is {value} the grand total?' (one of them `yes` x3), so the wording does not discriminate 'a total' from 'the total of the totals' and was not reworded, per the decision rule fixed before any call. The Note's own prose is therefore still not read or carried by this loop (spec § 6, 'What is not done'): the circa-85 gained tokens this register's 2026-08-20 note and the design spec both name as the live surface are still entirely inside this one escalated band, ignored rather than read. cbh therefore stays HELD: the score path no longer misses its four panel totals ([[R77]] closed on this evidence), but the document's one live escalation is unchanged and the grand total remains unbound." ] .

