    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5 (agent), task 5 of the 2026-08-20 arc-denominator loop; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD — recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. Escalation-reason census 2026-08-20 (HEAD 820ab24), § Seam 1: score 0.9720, 9 pages, ZERO escalation records on any of the nine reasons. § Token accounting for the same run reads 590 asserted / 17 escalated tokens. This document is the one the census names in its stated trap, § Method: RegionReport.reason is not reason-typed, and on ignored bands it carries the free-text CLASSIFICATION reason from regions._reason (strings such as fewer than 2 lines, fewer than 2 columns). ons books 70 of those and zero escalations. So a naive reason-count reads 70 problems here and a naive record-count reads a spotless document, and BOTH are wrong: neither number is about the reading. Nine pages of a statistical release with hierarchical SIC2007 section headers and a Total aggregate column have not been read against the compile by anyone, and this document carries no cor:contract / cor:terms / cor:shapes, so no membrane has ever seen its output. A score of 0.9720 on an unread nine-page document is precisely the shape of evidence this register exists to refuse to accept. Held." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Fable 5.1 (agent), the 2026-09-18 boxhead loop, on the maintainer's in-session direction to make ons the fourth accepted document; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD LIFTED — ACCEPTED at 0.8452535760728218, floor pinned at 0.84. The 2026-08-20 note above is NOT repaired in place (append-only register). What changed since the hold: the adopted data grids on p7 and p8 asserted 552 entry cells with NO column identity, and all 175 escalated tokens were header ink nothing read. The grid now carries its boxhead: a NEURAL reader proposes which header words head which column, answering in ADDRESSES only, and the proposal is disposed on every compile by the grid's own column intervals (src/iladub/etkl/boxhead.py: address space, total accounting of every listed word, per-label placement). 12 of 12 columns are labelled across the two pages, none dropped, text read back from the text layer; asserted ink 590 -> 650, escalated 175 -> 119. The compile is reproducible OFFLINE from the recorded readings under readings/boxhead/, which is what makes a floor pinnable at all. WHAT THE REMAINING 119 ESCALATED TOKENS ARE, stated so the acceptance is not read as a claim they are handled: the p0 release masthead and contents list (16, KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED — it is not a table and is honestly escalated), the p7 table title whose glyph runs are mangled in the text layer (19), and the two grids' residue (33 + 34): the spanning label over columns 1-5, which the reader reports and nothing yet disposes, and the in-table section captions. None of it is a misread entry. The floor is a regression guard under this accepted reading, not a lowered bar: the score it replaces, 0.9720, was computed over a denominator that excluded 142 tokens of this very ink." ] .

