    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5 (agent), task 5 of the 2026-08-20 arc-denominator loop; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD — recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned; 0.3556 is a measurement, and pinning it would move this rung without improving one reading. Escalation-reason census 2026-08-20 (HEAD 820ab24), § Seam 1: score 0.3556, 3 pages, 11 escalation records GRAPH-SIDE. § Token accounting for the same run reads 165 asserted / 299 escalated tokens. Census § Where the escalations actually are: REGION_TILING_FAILED x4 on p0 and x4 on p2 (the cash-flow and income statements), MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS x1 on p0 and x1 on p2 (the Three Months Ended … Nine Months Ended double header), DATAGRID_RESIDUE x1 on p1 under the adoption doc URI (document.py:1473). TWO DEFECTS ACCOUNT FOR TEN OF THE ELEVEN: one tiling failure repeated across the two statement pages, and one double header the matrix reader cannot resolve, firing once on each page it appears on. The eleventh is the adopted page leaving residue. Eleven investigations would be nine too many. This document is also the corpus's ONLY graph-side / report-side divergence, census § Graph-side vs report-side: on p1 five escalations are WITHDRAWN from the graph when the data grid supersedes them, while the RegionReport keeps its original reason — so report-side reads 16 reason-bearing reports on apple and the graph keeps 11, and the withdrawn set is REGION_TILING_FAILED x3, KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED x1, ROUND_TRIP_FAIL x1, replaced by the one DATAGRID_RESIDUE. Any later criterion that counts this document must say which side it counts; a SHACL membrane over the compiled graph can only ever see the 11. Held." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "Claude Sonnet (agent), task 5 of the 2026-09-02 the-body-starts-at-the-stub loop; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-09-02"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "STILL HOLD — recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. The 2026-08-20 note above is NOT repaired in place (append-only register); its 'one double header the matrix reader cannot resolve' framing is SUPERSEDED, not its measurements. The-body-starts-at-the-stub loop (matrix_body_start, `vocab/queries/matrix-body-start.rq`) derives the matrix body start from the first stub-bearing line rather than the raw header/body type split. MEASURED 2026-09-02 (Task 5, tests/etkl/test_apple_statement_headers.py, over two rounds — the first round found a gate defect, a controller ruling in commit 80f0cdf fixed it, and this rationale records the SECOND round's measurement against the fix): p0's income-statement header band ASSERTS — three levels (Three/Nine Months Ended over June 27,/June 28, over 2026/2025), 28 entries, region_tiles True — where it previously escalated MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS. p1's balance-sheet header band ALSO ASSERTS — two levels (June 27,/September 27, over 2026/2025), 14 entries, region_tiles True; this needed commit 80f0cdf (Task 3b, spec § 3.1 / § 8), which moved BOTH `is_matrix_candidate`'s and `classify_matrix`'s `>= 2` header-level gate to count levels at the DERIVED `matrix_body_start` instead of the raw `header_body_split` result — p1's band has type_split=1 (the years line 2026/2025 carries no stub, the identical class of defect p0 has) but a stub-bearing body_start=2, and the pre-fix gates refused it on the raw split before matrix_body_start ever ran. p2 band 2 (the unruled supplemental cash-flow header) still escalates MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS, for an HONEST reason: 'Nine Months Ended' is three separate pdfplumber words on a band with zero vertical rules, and infer_column_tree_by_proximity refuses rather than silently dropping 'Months' and both 'June's, which would win no column and be carried by no node (spec § 1.3 Finding B, § 3.2). Consequence, now MEASURED as spec § 1.4 predicted: the page-1 datagrid adoption IS pre-empted — adoption-candidate.rq's NOT EXISTS tab:EntryCell gate fires because p1's header now asserts a tab:EntryCell, so `adopted` moves `(1,) -> ()` (R160's premise — an asserting p1 header — now holds; its reader-authority question is live, not moot). MEASURED score (baseline.py, Task 1's instrument): 0.18950437317784258, down from the 2026-08-20 note's 0.3556 measurement and from Task 1's own re-measurement of 0.3587 at this loop's base commit — p0 and p1 each moved one region from escalated/superseded to asserted, and the whole-page adoption's synthetic RECORD_TABLE + DATAGRID_RESIDUE regions no longer exist, so several previously-superseded band verdicts on p1 revert to their own individually-escalated readings (REGION_TILING_FAILED x3, ROUND_TRIP_FAIL x1). The score is a measurement, not an acceptance (spec § 1.4); held until p1's header and the unruled p2 header are read by a human against the source page, and until R160's reader-authority question (band reader vs whole-page reader, now genuinely exercised on this document) is settled." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "Claude Opus 5 (agent), task 5 of the 2026-09-04 the-run-is-one-band loop (R165); the accountable human sign-off is Francois Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-09-04"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "STILL HOLD - recorded, not accepted. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated and no cor:scoreFloor is pinned. Neither note above is repaired in place (append-only register); their measurements stand, and the 2026-09-02 note's framing of p0/p1 as two separately-asserting header bands is SUPERSEDED, not refuted. The-run-is-one-band loop (R165) makes compile.page_bands PROPOSE a contiguous run of ruled bands as ONE band - vocab/queries/band-run.rq, an open-world derivation over sectiongraph.run_evidence's per-page graph, joining two ADJACENT ruled bands when one's set of distinct rounded rule x-positions subsumes the other's - and lets the EXISTING closed-world tiling membrane (compile.merged_run_admissible: is_matrix_candidate, classify_matrix, assert_matrix_region, region_tiles, on a scratch graph that is discarded) DISPOSE of the proposal. MEASURED 2026-09-04 on the SHIPPED tree with compile_document - not on the prototype that the spec and both spike documents report: document score 0.6288659793814433, up from the 2026-09-02 note's 0.18950437317784258. Per page: p0 1.0 (asserted=124, escalated=0), p1 1.0 (asserted=56, escalated=0), p2 0.027027 (asserted=3, escalated=108) - UNCHANGED, because p2's proposed run 3..7 is REFUSED at is_matrix_candidate. p0's bands 2..7 and p1's bands 2..7 are each one accepted run: eight page bands become three, the merged band occupies index 2 and mints the #mtable2 IRI that band 2 already minted, and the whole statement is read as ONE matrix - 124 and 56 entries against 48 and 14 cells at the previous baseline. The score is a MEASUREMENT, not an acceptance (the standing rule), and TWO things must be read beside it before anyone cites the rise. FIRST, p0 and p1 are now SATURATED at 1.0, which is a loss of signal and not only a gain: 1.0 is the ceiling, so no future regression on either page can be detected by its score again, and 63 of p1's 119 band words are counted on NEITHER side of the ratio - the stub column the matrix-asserted branch has always excluded, a pre-existing convention this loop neither introduced nor repaired. SECOND, the corpus-wide guard is that no page loses asserted ink: MEASURED over all 27 pages of all 7 documents, exactly two entries move and both move UP (apple p0 48 -> 124, apple p1 14 -> 56); the other 25 pages are unchanged. THE MEMBRANE HAS NOW SEEN A MERGED BAND, which nothing before this loop had ever measured: compile_document with validate_shapes=True returns the IDENTICAL 0.6288659793814433, so the merged holon crosses the contract membrane unrefused. R160 is NOT ruled by this loop: adopted is () both before and after, so the one-band reading makes the page-1 adoption UNNECESSARY rather than restoring it, and the reader-authority question stays open. R166's p0 half is disposed of (band 4's operating-income row becomes a leaf row of the merged matrix) and its p2 half survives. Held until p2's unruled header is read by a human against the source page, and until R160 is settled." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Fable 5.1 (agent), the 2026-09-18 apple boxhead loop, on the maintainer's in-session direction to bring apple to acceptance by the method that accepted ons; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD LIFTED — ACCEPTED at 0.9418604651162791, floor pinned at 0.94. None of the three notes above is repaired in place (append-only register). Every defect they held on has since been repaired by its own loop and none fires today: REGION_TILING_FAILED x8 and MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS x2 (the 2026-08-20 census) are gone — p0's income statement asserts 124 cells and p1's balance sheet 56 through the band path, with their multi-level headers, and p2's cash-flow statement asserts 87 cells through the adopted data grid. The single remaining escalation is that grid's own DATAGRID_RESIDUE. What this loop added: the p2 grid asserted its entries with NO column identity (datagrid.py derives entries only); it now carries its boxhead — 'June 27, 2026' over column 1 and 'June 28, 2025' over column 2 — proposed by the NEURAL boxhead reader in ADDRESSES only and disposed on every compile by the grid's own column intervals (src/iladub/etkl/boxhead.py), reproducible OFFLINE from the recording under readings/boxhead/. Asserted ink 480 -> 486, escalated 36 -> 30. WHAT THE REMAINING 30 ESCALATED TOKENS ARE, stated so the acceptance is not read as a claim they are handled: the statement's title block and unit line, the spanning label 'Nine Months Ended' over columns 1-2 (the reader reports it; nothing yet disposes a spanner's extent), and the in-table section captions ('Operating activities:', 'Investing activities:', 'Financing activities:' and their kin) — row-group headings the grid refuses as unplaceable and nothing yet reads. None is a misread entry." ] .

