#  appended at the end of the file for two reasons: the two cbh notes in the document block
#  above are not touched by a single character (their closing ` ] .` included), and no line
#  moves, so every arc-manifest prog:source line pointer into this file stays valid
#  (tests/test_arc_manifest.py::test_etkl_criterion_sources_point_at_the_document_they_name).
#  Turtle reads it as one more cor:adjudication on the same document.
#################################################################

<urn:iladub:corpus:cbh-stem-2026-08-03>
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "the ruling is the maintainer's, François Rosselet, 2026-10-02; composed by Claude Opus 5.5 (agent) in the cbh-hold-kept maintenance PR; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-10-02"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD KEPT, by the maintainer's ruling. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated, no cor:scoreFloor is pinned, and prog:criterion:etkl:03 stays unmet. This note does not supersede the 2026-08-20 or 2026-10-01 notes on this document, which are not repaired in place. WHAT MOVED (docs/superpowers/2026-10-02-r261-grand-total-evidence.md § 7): R261 loop (b) (PR #294) binds the grand total. `1,951,264` is now a total-of-totals tab:PrintedTotal (`…/p0/r2#printedtotal9-l0`) carrying no tab:totalOf, whose tab:aggregates are the four table-level PrintedTotals, produced by a decision gated on the worker's total_of_totals AND the exact Decimal sum 374904 + 737289 + 660363 + 178708 = 1951264 (§ 7.4). The escalation-furnish pin now reads 0 live escalations: 5 chose escalated, 5 superseded, 0 requests (§ 7.3). It was renamed in this change from test_corpus_cbh_furnishes_exactly_one_request_for_its_one_live_escalation_the_residue, the name the 2026-10-01 note cites, to tests/etkl/test_escalation_furnish.py::test_corpus_cbh_furnishes_no_request_its_residue_escalation_is_withdrawn_as_ignored. cbh's score moves 0.9107 -> 1.0 (0.9106957424714434 -> 1.0, § 7.1). WHY THE HOLD IS KEPT: of that +0.0893, only +0.0010 is the binding (one token moves from escalated to asserted, 877/963 -> 878/963). The other +0.0883 is the four-line Note leaving the denominator: once `1,951,264` is carved out of band 9, the remainder classifies NON_TABLE and lands in `…/p0/r2#ignored9`, classified rather than read ([[R288]]). The Note is the caveat the page prints on its four tables ('Dates are subject to change and are only a guide … only an estimate'). Discarding it violates CLAUDE.md core principle 5, context is carried, not discarded, so a 1.0 bought by dropping the page's own caveat is not an acceptance. NEXT: [[R288]], reading the Note as context carried on the tables it qualifies." ] .

#################################################################
#  cbh-stem — the maintainer's 2026-10-05 ruling: R288's close arm (b). Appended at the end for
#  the 2026-10-02 block's reasons: no earlier line changes, so every prog:source pointer into this
#  file stays valid.
#################################################################

<urn:iladub:corpus:cbh-stem-2026-08-03>
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "the ruling is the maintainer's, François Rosselet, 2026-10-05; composed by Claude Opus 5.5 (agent) on branch r288-scope-probe-live; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-10-05"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "R288 CLOSED BY RULING (its close arm (b)); THE HOLD IS NOT LIFTED. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated, no cor:scoreFloor is pinned, and prog:criterion:etkl:03 stays unmet. This note does not supersede the 2026-08-20, 2026-10-01 or 2026-10-02 notes, which are not repaired in place. THE RULING: ignoring cbh's four-line Note ('Dates are subject to change and are only a guide … only an estimate') is acceptable for etkl:03. The Note stays an etkl:IgnoredBand (`…/p0/r2#ignored9`), and its exit from the denominator stays worth +0.0883 of cbh's 0.9107 -> 1.0 (877/963 -> 878/878; the binding is +0.0010, 878/963). The 2026-10-02 note named this +0.0883 as the reason for keeping the hold, and this ruling removes that reason. WHY: the only route to carrying the Note is a reader that decides WHETHER an ignored band is a caveat on a table, and no oracle disposes that judgement. The scope probe (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-r288-scope-probe-refuted.md) ran the composite under a verdict rule fixed before any call and was REFUTED: 4 of 8 notes admitted, 5 non-notes, 3 nulls. The worker called 37 of the 40 parsed non-notes a note, and reading-order equality disposes only WHICH tables a note qualifies, never WHETHER it is one. Under the 2026-09-17 ruling (no oracle, no worker) that reader cannot ship. Designing a WHETHER oracle is parked until a second document style needs it, and re-prompting against the same 8-note truth set is refused because it would fit the prompt to the truth set. CLAUDE.md principle 5 (context is carried, not discarded) is knowingly not met for this one caveat, by this ruling. WHY THE HOLD STAYS: the maintainer ruled the hold separate from R288. Two things stand between cbh and acceptance. First, [[R74]] is open: the data grid leaks one row from the page's second table, and etkl:03 carries a proposed dependency on tab:01 for that reason. Second, no dated note records cbh's carried grid read against the source page, which graincorp-capacity's 2026-09-13 acceptance discharged by measurement. Lifting the hold is its own loop." ] .

