<urn:iladub:corpus:cbh-stem-2026-08-03>
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5.5 (agent) on branch cbh-carried-grid-read; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-10-05"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD KEPT; THE CARRIED GRID WAS READ AGAINST THE PAGE AND FOUND ONE DEFECT. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:Unadjudicated, no cor:scoreFloor is pinned, and prog:criterion:etkl:03 stays unmet. This note does not supersede the earlier notes, which are not repaired in place. It records the read the previous note asked for, done by measurement on graincorp-capacity's 2026-09-13 method (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-cbh-carried-grid-read.md). WHAT HOLDS, at 4d07b7c: 878 of 878 carried nodes' text equals the page ink inside their bbox; 0 of 1244 page words are unaccounted for; every entry cell and label lies inside a drawn column interval; nearest-printed-label column assignment agrees on 850 of 858 words, and the 8 disagreements are left-aligned TOTAL values and over-wide client names, neither of them a carriage error (a column-swap null control raises the count by exactly the two swapped cells); every port total equals the exact Decimal sum of its carried Volume cells. WHAT DOES NOT: R289. Each of the four port rosters carries a row r0 holding the header's bottom line (Accepted, Accepted, Completed, Completed) as tab:EntryCell data, 16 header words in 4 rows that have no vessel, while the labels for those columns carry only Time Nom, Date Nom, Date Loading and Time Loading. That is header ink carried as data and cannot be accepted. A CORRECTION TO THE PREVIOUS NOTE: its premise that the data grid leaks one row from the page's second table is FALSE at HEAD. derive_data_grid admits none of lines 75 to 80, no carried cell holds ink from the 1,951,264 line or the Note, and 1,951,264 is the total-of-totals tab:PrintedTotal. R74 stays open only because tab:StackedGrids is underived, which nothing in cbh's carriage depends on. Whether R74 still stands between cbh and acceptance is the maintainer's call. NEXT: R289." ] .

