#################################################################
#  cbh-stem — 2026-10-05, the maintainer's acceptance ruling. Appended at the end, so no earlier
#  line moves; the verdict and floor were set on the document block's own line 90, line-neutrally.
#################################################################

<urn:iladub:corpus:cbh-stem-2026-08-03>
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "ruled by François Rosselet (maintainer), 2026-10-05; composed by Claude Opus 5.5 (agent) on branch accept-cbh; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-10-05"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD LIFTED BY RULING; cbh IS ACCEPTED WITH R289 RECORDED AS A ROLE DEFECT. cor:expectedVerdict is now cor:CompilesAbove and cor:scoreFloor is pinned at 0.99, and prog:criterion:etkl:03 is met. This note does not supersede the earlier notes, which are not repaired in place. THE RULING applies the rule the maintainer already applied on 2026-10-05 to who-wfa, ons and apple (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-r289-split-on-a-line-with-no-data.md § 3 (c)): an acceptance stands with a role defect, provided the defect is recorded as a residue. cbh's only blocker was R289 (each port roster's r0 carries the header's bottom line, Accepted/Accepted/Completed/Completed, as tab:EntryCell data: 16 header words in 4 rows that have no vessel). It is the same kind of defect as the three already accepted: header ink carried in the wrong role, nothing fabricated, nothing dropped. The carried-grid read (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-cbh-carried-grid-read.md) found it the only defect: 878 of 878 carried nodes match the page ink inside their bbox, 0 of 1244 page words are unaccounted for. WHY NOW: R289 has taken six loops, each ending in a refuted premise, and the last one (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-r289-reader-undercounts-tree-overlaps.md) showed it is two defects in series: the typed split, and behind it the header tree (forcing the correct split drops cbh 1.0 -> 0.6929 on tab:NoOverlapShape). Fixing it would not move cbh's score, which is already 1.0; it would only move 16 words from data to header. WHAT THIS ACCEPTANCE DOES NOT SAY: that the rosters' column labels are complete (c4/c5/c18/c19 carry only the top line, e.g. Time Nom for Time Nom Accepted), or that the four r0 rows are vessel rows. Both stay open under R289, which stays in the register on its own terms. cor:scoreFloor is 0.99, not the measured 1.0, for R194's reason, as for graincorp-capacity: 1.0 is the ratio ceiling, and at 878 tokens 0.99 tolerates about 8 tokens of drift while catching any systematic regression. Measured score at main 6ed16d7: 1.0 (docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-r289-reader-undercounts-tree-overlaps.md § 2)." ;
        cor:recordedIn "docs/superpowers/2026-10-05-r289-reader-undercounts-tree-overlaps.md" ] .
